# Awesome Design – Portfolio Website  
Created by Mohammed Ali  

A responsive portfolio website showcasing my design work, wireframes, and validation evidence.  
This project was built using two open‑source Start Bootstrap templates and customised extensively to meet the Unit 1 requirements.

---

## 1. Project Overview

Awesome Design is a personal portfolio website created to demonstrate my ability to build a responsive, accessible, and professionally presented website.  
The site includes wireframes, portfolio items, contact information, and validation evidence.

The project is deployed on Neocities and fully responsive across desktop, tablet, and mobile devices.

Live Site: https://ali-design.neocities.org/  
GitHub Repo: https://github.com/Md12Ali/Awesome-Design  

---

## 2. UX (User Experience)

### **Strategy**
The goal of this project is to present my design work clearly and professionally while demonstrating strong web development fundamentals.

### **Target Users**
- Employers reviewing my portfolio  
- Tutors assessing my Unit 1 submission  
- Anyone interested in my design work  

### **User Needs**
- Easy navigation  
- Clear layout  
- Accessible content  
- Mobile‑friendly design  
- Visual examples of work  

---

## 3. User Stories

### **As a visitor, I want to:**
- View the portfolio easily on any device  
- Understand what the website is about immediately  
- Navigate between sections smoothly  
- See wireframes and validation evidence  
- Contact the creator via email  

### **As an assessor, I want to:**
- Verify accessibility (alt text, correct links, readable content)  
- Confirm correct documentation and attribution  
- See HTML and CSS validation results  
- Check that filenames and paths follow best practice  

---

